# {{SITE_NAME}}

{{PURPOSE}}

A DjangoCMS 5 site (Bootstrap 5.3, light/dark mode, mobile friendly) scaffolded by the
`djangocms-agent` skill. It ships a landing page, an About page and a "Style & Capabilities" page that
renders every verified plugin.

## Quick start

    python3 -m venv venv
    venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt
    export DJANGO_DEBUG=1 DJANGO_SECRET_KEY=dev
    venv/bin/python manage.py migrate
    venv/bin/python manage.py createsuperuser
    venv/bin/python manage.py seed_pages
    venv/bin/python manage.py seed_site
    venv/bin/python manage.py runserver 8010

Open http://localhost:8010/ (use the first free port at or above 8000; check with `ss -ltn`) and sign in at http://localhost:8010/admin/. Edit pages by adding
`?edit` to a URL while logged in. `DJANGO_DEBUG=1` is development only; production needs
`DJANGO_SECRET_KEY` and `DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS` (see `.env.example`).

## Verify

    bin/verify.sh

Runs `check`, `makemigrations --check`, the tests, seed idempotency, and Playwright screenshots
(desktop and mobile) of the main pages into `verify-shots/`. Look at them. Requires
Playwright for the visual step; install it once in a scratch venv, not system Python:

    python3 -m venv /tmp/pw-venv && /tmp/pw-venv/bin/pip install playwright && /tmp/pw-venv/bin/playwright install chromium
    PLAYWRIGHT_PYTHON=/tmp/pw-venv/bin/python bin/verify.sh

Without it `bin/verify.sh` ends `VERIFY RESULT: INCOMPLETE`. The verification server runs with
`DJANGO_DEBUG_TOOLBAR=0`.

{{DOCKER_README}}## Known warnings and development extras

- `treebeard.E001` (a warning about `cms.PageManager`) is printed on every `manage.py` command. It comes
  from django-cms 5.1.3 with django-treebeard 5.3.x, is upstream, and is harmless until treebeard 6; do not
  try to fix it in this project.
- With `DJANGO_DEBUG=1` a small green tab on the right edge of pages is the django-debug-toolbar handle (not
  the CMS toolbar). It only exists when DEBUG is on; set `DJANGO_DEBUG_TOOLBAR=0` to remove it.

